			"fileName": "generative-proof-of-concept-CPU-preprocessing-in-memory.py",
			"wiki": "A base model architecture is defined. It includes a standard token embedding layer followed by an `InterleavedRoPE` layer. `InterleavedRoPE` applies rotary positional embeddings, which is an efficient way to encode token position information, especially for long sequences.",
			"cellName": "Define Base Model with RoPE - generative-proof-of-concept-CPU-preprocessing-in-memory.py:L272-298",
			"cellId": "b8cd8864-82fe-433c-afc1-32ca69c6050b",
