			"fileName": "regression-example-ames-no-preproc-val-set.py",
			"wiki": "The `hash_a_row` function converts all cells in the row to strings, concatenates them, computes a standard hash, and returns the absolute (unsigned) value. This ensures that identical rows always produce the same hash.",
			"cellName": "Compute Row Hash - regression-example-ames-no-preproc-val-set.py:L35-40",
