		"cerebros/simplecerebrosrandomsearch/simple_cerebros_random_search.py-simstep-5fd2a0e4-8911-4a15-b354-dc6fe1faeda9": {
			"path": "cerebros/simplecerebrosrandomsearch/simple_cerebros_random_search.py-simstep-5fd2a0e4-8911-4a15-b354-dc6fe1faeda9",
			"fileName": "simple_cerebros_random_search.py",
			"wiki": "The Keras `model.fit()` function receives the training data, along with `validation_split=0.0` and the custom `validation_data`. Keras's internal logic prioritizes `validation_data` when it is provided, using it for validation metrics and ignoring the `validation_split` parameter. This completes the use case by training on one pre-split set and evaluating on another.",
			"cellName": "Train Model with Custom Validation Set - simple_cerebros_random_search.py:L498-505",
			"cellId": "a79e41fc-2d5a-4f1e-809f-023e9198ca61",
			"visible": true,
