			"description": "<ul><li>Automatically finds optimal neural network architectures for regression or classification tasks on structured, tabular data</li><li>Users provide a dataset (e</li><li>g</li><li>, CSV file), define input/output shapes, and specify a metric to optimize (e</li><li>g</li><li>, <code>val_root_mean_squared_error</code>)</li><li>Cerebros explores a complex search space of biologically-inspired networks with randomized vertical (skip) and lateral connections to find a high-performing model</li><li>The primary entry point is the <code>SimpleCerebrosRandomSearch</code> class, demonstrated in <code>regression-example-ames-no-preproc</li><li>py</code></li></ul>",
